# The tolerance a rendered case must meet to PASS.
#
# max-diff     the largest per-channel difference (0 to 255) allowed anywhere
# max-bad-ppm  pixels differing by more than 1/255 in any channel, in parts per
#              million of the pixels
# evidence     the row of the oracle tolerance table that supports the pair
#              (documentation/conformance.md), or "none" while it is zero
#
# The tolerance is a finding, not a guess: shape-cpu's coverage is exact area, the
# references are palette-reduced PNGs, and each oracle anti-aliases differently, so no
# renderer matches them to the bit. The pair is where the planted defects of
# tolerance_planted.py (a shift of a tenth of a pixel, a 0.2% growth, a 2% fade) are
# all still refused; documentation/conformance.md, "The tolerance pair", has the
# sweep. `make tolerance-planted` shows it refuse them. score.py fails on a nonzero
# pair whose evidence is "none".
max-diff	32
max-bad-ppm	2000
evidence	conformance.md, "The tolerance pair"
